                <pb facs="0326" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1631/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-29T12:00:00-06:00">September 29,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Your telegram No. 58, September 28, 6 p.m. to the Legation in Managua.<anchor
                        n="37" xml:id="d265-f1"/> Proposed trade agreement will require ratification
                    by the Salvadoran Legislature. Its next session will be inaugurated early next
                    February and will last for several months.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
